# Private display standard-entry integration evidence

Baseline 41a8435ecd2f21b7e78f7dce7ec2915386cfff83. This directory preserves raw bytes and local input/output consistency for two-architecture validation tools and read-only display configuration. It does not authenticate a user able to rewrite the whole evidence bundle.

Both architectures built nine targets from seventeen bound compiler inputs using CMake 4.2.3, MSVC 19.44.35226.0/v143 and Windows SDK 10.0.19041.0. The x86 compiler body exited 0; its external owned supervisor remained false/124 after a reported vctip tail was precisely cleaned. No compiler-tail policy is applied or retrospectively claimed. The x64 preparation closed naturally. The preparation manifest deliberately requires separate external caller evidence.

All eight protocol/native/tail group supervisors and both display collectors closed naturally. Passing tail behavior suites contain intentional negative fixture Jobs, whose false results remain in raw records. The only protocol skip is the preexisting serializer case; native groups have no skips. Display records bind native PID/FILETIME, context, raw report and exact PE hashes. Configuration success carries no presentation, optical calibration, performance or release claim.

The default entry runs pure reader tests. Real configuration collection requires explicit opt-in. Actual PowerShell AST and Collect block projections verify optional wiring; neither full Test nor full Collect ran. Pure preparation PE fixtures are authored metadata and do not establish native compilation. Old RED and failed harness runs remain separate. Historical fixture recovery is identified and hash-checked in source-snapshot-map files.

current-map.json binds exact copied current raw/canonical build configuration to original paths. Compiled EXE/obj/lib/pdb and any MSBuild binlog stay private, hash-only, rather than source evidence. Code and generated metadata copies use .inert.snapshot; their bytes are unchanged. No GUI, ETW, SendInput, VM, complete SDK build, Win7/PE matrix, soak or release acceptance was executed. Root owns subsequent documentation, Git integration and persistent archive.
